vitals-ssl: a client callback for a server's certificate request, with the CA names it
accepts (TLS 1.2's CertificateRequest and TLS 1.3's certificate_authorities extension), whose
certificate for the handshake is the one sent, so a connection picks its client certificate as
Sony's libssl does (vitals-ssl/src/connection.c). Applied to the Mbed TLS 3.6 release, after
offer-unknown-ciphersuites.patch, by crypto/apply_patch.cmake

--- a/include/mbedtls/ssl.h
+++ b/include/mbedtls/ssl.h
